# InsightFace model weights (~300MB, downloaded on first run)
/ml/models/
~/.insightface/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BIOMETRIC / PERSONAL DATA — never commit any of this.
#
# ml/eval/datasets holds real event photographs and the selfies of real, named
# people; ml/eval/cache holds the face templates computed from them. Under GDPR
# Art. 9 those are special-category personal data. A git repository is
# permanent, replicated and in practice un-deletable, which is the exact
# opposite of every retention guarantee in docs/COMPLIANCE.md. Committing here
# would be a personal data breach on its own.
#
# Reports are the exception and are meant to be committed: they hold counts and
# aggregate scores, never an embedding, a crop or a filename. A test asserts
# that (tests/test_eval_end_to_end.py::test_report_contains_no_embeddings), and
# config/thresholds.toml records the SHA-256 of the report that justified it, so
# the evidence has to travel with the code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ml/eval/datasets/
/ml/eval/cache/
*.npz
*.npy
.dev/
.storage/
